Subject: [PATCH 123/638] [AROS] Use uncaged cppgc before sparse MMU
 reservations

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3
AI_STATUS: complete
ROOT_CAUSE: Hosted run 0123 exhausted the pre-MMU physical allocator while V8 attempted cppgc's sparse 8-17 GiB cage reservation.
FIX_REASON: Advance the pinned V8 port to its AROS uncaged-cppgc commit, preserving a replayable boundary between the engine configuration and Chromium integration.
SCOPE: v8 submodule pointer
VALIDATION: V8 cppgc_base cross-compiled 105 affected targets without cage, young-generation, or cppgc pointer-compression defines.
RISK: This intentionally trades cppgc cage-derived optimizations for a functional pre-MMU bring-up; the cage should return once OPAL provides sparse virtual reservations.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: run 0123 cage OOM -> V8 91d3ac5a3c -> hosted run 0124
---
 v8 | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v8 b/v8
index 35a278897f..91d3ac5a3c 160000
--- a/v8
+++ b/v8
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 35a278897fa08a1be8adc13c72fae8ceca010c01
+Subproject commit 91d3ac5a3cb542a5bdcc54e5af4623a101264c55
